Subject: [PATCH 2/2] [DS4.1] Attention: the decode front's one kernel in the
 forward

At decode rows with cache pages (no sequence parallelism, no breakable
graphs), the attention forward runs attention_front after the fused Q-A/KV
projection: it writes the normalized q latent and its MXFP8 cast, and the
rotated kv latent's SWA record, so the separate norms, cast, kv RoPE and
cache write do not launch. Q-B now reads its input's cast from the input's
producer: the front kernel's, or cast_mxfp8 (the per_token_cast it ran itself
before) on every other path.

Test: the routing (decode rows run the one kernel at the SWA slots and page
size and hand Q-B its cast; sequence-parallel rows, rows past a decode tile
and memory profiling do not).
---
 tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_attention.py | 38 +++++++++
 vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/attention.py       | 83 ++++++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 115 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

